  <static seed="1759" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/SignedNumbersArithemtic/DivideWithNegativeIntegers10.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\frac{-28}{-4}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{56}{-7}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{-45}{9}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The rules for dividing positive numbers are the same as those for multiplication:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{positive} \div \text{positive} = \text{positive} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{positive} \div \text{negative} = \text{negative} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{negative} \div \text{positive} = \text{negative} }</m>,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{negative} \div \text{negative} = \text{positive} }</m>.</p>
<p>The solutions are:</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{-28}{-4}={7},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{56}{-7}={-8},  }</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \frac{-45}{9}={-5}.  }</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
